    "title": "Tigers look to keep rolling at home against South Dakota - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joseph Pastilha, Columbia Missourian ,\n6 hours ago Mizzou welcomes South Dakota to Mizzou Arena Thursday night as it looks to pick up its seventh straight win to start to the season. South Dakota (3-2) is entering the matchup having won its last three games following an 0-2 start to the season. The Coyotes have found success offensively, averaging 89.6 points per game in the young season. Junior guard Isaac Bruns has led South Dakota on the scoresheet with an average of just over 17 points per game. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
